menu "CSI Pair Configuration"

    config CSI_PAIR_ID
        int "CSI pair ID (1-255, last byte of the pair MAC)"
        range 1 255
        default 1
        help
            Each sender/receiver pair must have a unique pair ID. The sender sets its
            station MAC to 1a:00:00:00:00:<PAIR_ID>, and the receiver only accepts CSI
            frames whose source MAC matches, so pairs do not pick up each other's CSI.

    config CSI_CHANNEL
        int "WiFi channel used by this pair (1-13)"
        range 1 13
        default 11
        help
            Pairs running at the same time and place should use different channels
            (e.g. 1 / 6 / 11) to reduce co-channel interference. The sender and the
            receiver of ONE pair must use the same channel.

endmenu
